  "id": "DrugBank_DB01132 - MONDO_5015",
  "verbalization": "Pioglitazone is clinically indicated for Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus, and its relationship with the disease is supported by multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to the disease through the indication of Voglibose, Nateglinide, and Vildagliptin, all of which are indicated for Diabetes Mellitus. These pathways suggest that Pioglitazone may exert a modulatory effect on the disease process through a mechanism that involves the regulation of glucose metabolism or insulin sensitivity. The presence of multiple indirect pathways with high scores indicates a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, mechanism by which Pioglitazone could influence the pathophysiology of Diabetes Mellitus. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Pioglitazone may have a role in the management of the disease, though further mechanistic investigation is needed to confirm its therapeutic potential.",
